lass="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S2.Ex7.m1.pic1.53" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\crvi</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(13.16,-28.26)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.33em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.96" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="4.61"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">-</span></span></foreignObject><foreignObject overflow="visible"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S2.Ex7.m1.pic1.54" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\crvi</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(8.31,-26.8)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.33em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.96" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="4.61"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">-</span></span></foreignObject><foreignObject overflow="visible"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S2.Ex7.m1.pic1.55" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\crvi</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(3.46,-25.35)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.33em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.96" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="4.61"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">-</span></span></foreignObject><foreignObject overflow="visible"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S2.Ex7.m1.pic1.56" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\crvi</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS8.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We will briefly explain the interpretation of <math id="S2.SS8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{\Delta_{\rm irr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>irr</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{\Delta_{\rm irr}}</annotation></semantics></math> for the reader’s convenience. The vertex <math id="S2.SS8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in\Gamma_{\Delta_{\rm irr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>irr</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in\Gamma_{\Delta_{\rm irr}}</annotation></semantics></math> is unlabeled, so implicitly it has genus <math id="S2.SS8.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, both edges emanating from <math id="S2.SS8.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> are unramified, therefore the degree <math id="S2.SS8.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.SS8.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S2.SS8.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>. So the rational curve associated to <math id="S2.SS8.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is attached to the curve <math id="S2.SS8.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> at two points. The stable model of the domain curve is therefore an irreducible nodal curve, hence the label “<math id="S2.SS8.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\rm irr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>irr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\rm irr}</annotation></semantics></math>”.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS8.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.8.1 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In practice, the boundary divisors <math id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\rm irr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>irr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\rm irr}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{D}}_{\rm adm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>adm</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{D}}_{\rm adm}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{T}}_{\rm adm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>adm</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{T}}_{\rm adm}</annotation></semantics></math> occur most frequently in one parameter families. We will often suppress the subscript and refer to the latter two as <math id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For simplicity, we adopt the following convention: <span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">The symbols <math id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> will denote the divisors parameterizing covers having <math id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2,2)</annotation></semantics></math>-ramification and triple ramification, respectively, regardless of the compactification we work in.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Because of the scarcity of interaction with other boundary divisors, we refer to any boundary divisor which is not any of the above three as a <span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">higher boundary divisor</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">2.9 Partial pencil families.</h3>

<div id="S2.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section introduces the class of one parameter families central to the rest of the paper. We call these families <span id="S2.SS9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">partial pencil</span> families, and they lie entirely within the boundary of <math id="S2.SS9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}</annotation></semantics></math> (or <math id="S2.SS9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>adm</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rmk">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 2.5</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To aid the reader, we mention that our one parameter families will always begin as families in <math id="S2.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>adm</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then if necessary will be lifted to <math id="S2.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is the main purpose of <a href="#S2.Thmthm4" title="Lemma 2.4. ‣ 2.7 
          
            
              
              
                ¯
                H
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  d
                  ,
                  g
                
              
            
          
         vs. 
          
            
              
              
                
                
                  ¯
                  H
                
                adm
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  d
                  ,
                  g
                
              
            
          
        . ‣ 2 Compactifications. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First we give an informal description of a partial pencil. Consider a boundary component <math id="S2.SS9.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\subset\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>adm</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\subset\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The general admissible cover parametrized by <math id="S2.SS9.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</p>
<table id="S2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha{\colon}C_{L}\cup C_{R}\longrightarrow P_{L}\cup P_{R}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha{\colon}C_{L}\cup C_{R}\longrightarrow P_{L}\cup P_{R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS9.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS9.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{L}{\colon}C_{L}\longrightarrow P_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{L}{\colon}C_{L}\longrightarrow P_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS9.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{R}{\colon}C_{R}\longrightarrow P_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{R}{\colon}C_{R}\longrightarrow P_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> are the left and right sides of the admissible cover. The essential idea behind the partial pencil families is to vary one of the maps, which we typically take to be the right hand side <math id="S2.SS9.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, while keeping the left map <math id="S2.SS9.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> (including the points of attachment) fixed in moduli.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rmk">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 2.6</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The reader may find it useful to think of partial pencils as the <math id="S2.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S2.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>adm</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}</annotation></semantics></math> analogues of the standard one parameter families of curves found in the boundary of <math id="S2.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g}}</annotation></semantics></math>. One major difference is that in the case of <math id="S2.Thmthm6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g}}</annotation></semantics></math> there exist, conveniently, complete one parameter families lying entirely within a single boundary component while avoiding all others. Unfortunately, partial pencil families typically intersect other boundary components; the management of their intersection with other boundary components is the ultimate technical obstacle in this paper.</p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS9.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.9.1 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now we give a formal description. Fix a partition <math id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{r}=r_{1}+r_{2}+...+r_{k}=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{r}=r_{1}+r_{2}+...+r_{k}=d</annotation></semantics></math> by positive integers <math id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose</p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.E1.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="64.83" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-50.966255691547325px" version="1.1" viewBox="13.69 50.97 101.64 64.83" width="101.64"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 13.686396924888871 64.83015453929276) translate(0,3.46) translate(13.69,0)"><g transform="translate(-13.69,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.38em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="19.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.E1.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{\mathcal{C}}_{R}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{\mathcal{C}}_{R}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 13.686396924888871 -0.27673578005007266 L 13.686396924888871 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(25.62,0) translate(0,6.93) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.09em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.56" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="15.02"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.E1.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\alpha_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">α</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\alpha_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(61.16,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 13.686396924888871 -0.27673578005007266 L 61.158607391066056 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 61.158607391066056 -0.27673578005007266 L 61.158607391066056 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 8.35219705617822 -9.685900096859001 L 8.38870244747345 -9.714994619244672" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-3.9,0) translate(0,-28.98) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-2.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.03em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="14.31"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.E1.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{f_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">f</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{f_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(28.67,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -2.43 7.05" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.62 3.43" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 8.35219705617822 -9.685900096859001 L 28.672609583906272 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 28.636104192611043 -33.18069814827427 L 28.672609583906272 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(61.16,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.34em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="18.49"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.E1.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{\mathcal{P}}_{R}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{\mathcal{P}}_{R}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 66.2612967823029 -9.685900096859001 L 66.25901651494613 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(55.99,0) translate(0,-27.82) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.14)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.98em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.05" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="13.53"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.E1.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{p_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">p</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{p_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(46.11,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 6.6 3.45" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 2.4 7.05" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 66.2612967823029 -9.685900096859001 L 46.1129388720791 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 46.11521913943588 -33.208800332088 L 46.1129388720791 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(28.63,0) translate(0,-43.36) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.67em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="9.28"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.E1.m1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{S}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is a one parameter family of <math id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{r}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">-marked</span> admissible covers parameterized by a smooth, proper curve <math id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. This means</p>
<ol id="S2.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite map from the nodal family of genus <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> curves <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> to the nodal family of genus <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> curves <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is a marked section <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf 0}\subset{\mathcal{P}}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf 0}\subset{\mathcal{P}}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, disjoint from the singular locus of the map <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</p>
<table id="S2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{-1}({\bf 0})=r_{1}R_{1}\sqcup r_{2}R_{2}\sqcup...\sqcup r_{k}R_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⊔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⊔</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>⊔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{-1}({\bf 0})=r_{1}R_{1}\sqcup r_{2}R_{2}\sqcup...\sqcup r_{k}R_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I3.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}{\colon}S\longrightarrow{\mathcal{C}}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}{\colon}S\longrightarrow{\mathcal{C}}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> are sections disjoint from <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Sing}(f_{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Sing</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Sing}(f_{R})</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, the family (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2.9.1 ‣ 2.9 Partial pencil families. ‣ 2 Compactifications. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>) is ramified over <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>𝟎</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf 0}</annotation></semantics></math> according to the partition given by <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Away from <math id="S2.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>𝟎</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf 0}</annotation></semantics></math> and the singular locus <math id="S2.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Sing}(p_{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Sing</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Sing}(p_{R})</annotation></semantics></math>, the map <math id="S2.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is simply-branched.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Above <math id="S2.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Sing}(p_{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Sing</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Sing}(p_{R})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> must satisfy the usual admissible cover “kissing” condition.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">(Note: An <math id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{r}</annotation></semantics></math>-marked admissible cover is very similar to an admissible cover - we simply allow for higher ramification, given by the profile <math id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, above a specified marked point <math id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>𝟎</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf 0}</annotation></semantics></math> in the target.)</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS9.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.9.2 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, fix a single <math id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{r}</annotation></semantics></math>-marked cover <math id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{L}{\colon}C_{L}\longrightarrow(P_{L},{\bf 0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{L}{\colon}C_{L}\longrightarrow(P_{L},{\bf 0})</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}T_{1}+r_{2}T_{2}+...+r_{k}T_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}T_{1}+r_{2}T_{2}+...+r_{k}T_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> be the preimage of <math id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf 0}\in P_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf 0}\in P_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{L}:=C_{L}\times S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{L}:=C_{L}\times S</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}_{L}:=P_{L}\times S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}_{L}:=P_{L}\times S</annotation></semantics></math>. We let <math id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}=T_{i}\times S\subset{\mathcal{C}}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}=T_{i}\times S\subset{\mathcal{C}}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the section along which <math id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is ramified to order <math id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS9.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.9.3 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS9.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, let <math id="S2.SS9.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the surface obtained by identifying <math id="S2.SS9.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.SS9.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S2.SS9.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,...,k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,...,k</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, let <math id="S2.SS9.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the surface obtained by glueing <math id="S2.SS9.SSS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf 0}\in{\mathcal{P}}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf 0}\in{\mathcal{P}}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.SS9.SSS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf 0}\in{\mathcal{P}}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf 0}\in{\mathcal{P}}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this way, we construct a family of admissible covers</p>
<table id="S2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha{\colon}{\mathcal{C}}\longrightarrow{\mathcal{P}}\longrightarrow S." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha{\colon}{\mathcal{C}}\longrightarrow{\mathcal{P}}\longrightarrow S.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.7</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Partial pencil)<span id="S2.Thmthm7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">partial pencil</span> is any one-parameter family of admissible covers <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha{\colon}{\mathcal{C}}\longrightarrow{\mathcal{P}}\longrightarrow S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha{\colon}{\mathcal{C}}\longrightarrow{\mathcal{P}}\longrightarrow S</annotation></semantics></math> as constructed above. We call <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{R}{\colon}{\mathcal{C}}_{R}\longrightarrow{\mathcal{P}}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{R}{\colon}{\mathcal{C}}_{R}\longrightarrow{\mathcal{P}}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>) the <span id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">right side</span> (resp. <span id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">left side</span>) of the partial pencil <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. We call the <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}\subset{\mathcal{C}}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}\subset{\mathcal{C}}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}\subset{\mathcal{C}}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}\subset{\mathcal{C}}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>) the <span id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">right gluing sections</span> (resp. <span id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">left gluing sections</span>).</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS9.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that the left side of a partial pencil is fixed in moduli. (Including the points of attachment.)</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS9.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.9.4 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS9.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="S2.SS9.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\longrightarrow\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>adm</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\longrightarrow\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a partial pencil family, lying entirely within a boundary divisor <math id="S2.SS9.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>. By <a href="#S2.Thmthm4" title="Lemma 2.4. ‣ 2.7 
          
            
              
              
                ¯
                H
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  d
                  ,
                  g
                
              
            
          
         vs. 
          
            
              
              
                
                
                  ¯
                  H
                
                adm
              
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  d
                  ,
                  g
                
              
            
          
        . ‣ 2 Compactifications. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>, we may lift this family to a family <math id="S2.SS9.SSS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}\longrightarrow\Delta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}\longrightarrow\Delta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S2.SS9.SSS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\prime}\subset\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\prime}\subset\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}</annotation></semantics></math> lying over <math id="S2.SS9.SSS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\subset\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>adm</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\subset\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Such families <math id="S2.SS9.SSS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}\longrightarrow\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}\longrightarrow\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}</annotation></semantics></math> will be called <span id="S2.SS9.SSS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">twisted partial pencils</span>. In particular, the coarse space of a twisted partial pencil is a partial pencil.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS10" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">2.10 Intersection multiplicities.</h3>

<div id="S2.SS10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now indicate how to compute intersection multiplicities of a one parameter family lying entirely in the boundary with boundary divisors. For this, we review the description of the deformation spaces of admissible covers found in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx20" title="" class="ltx_ref">HM82</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS10.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.10.1 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Pick any boundary divisor <math id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\subset\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>adm</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\subset\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and choose a general admissible cover <math id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[\alpha\colon C\longrightarrow P]\in\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\alpha\colon C\longrightarrow P]\in\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in P</annotation></semantics></math> be the unique node, and let <math id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r_{1},r_{2},...,r_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r_{1},r_{2},...,r_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> be the local degrees of <math id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> occurring at the nodes <math id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{1},...,q_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{1},...,q_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> above <math id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>. A description of the complete local ring <math id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{{\mathcal{O}}}_{\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}},\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>adm</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{{\mathcal{O}}}_{\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}},\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by Harris and Mumford in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx20" title="" class="ltx_ref">HM82</a>]</cite> as:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{{\mathcal{O}}}_{\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}},\alpha}={\text{\rm Spec}\,}k[[z_{1},...,z_{b-4},t_{1},t_{2},...,t_{k},s]]/(t_{1}^{r_{1}}=t_{2}^{r_{2}}=...=t_{k}^{r_{k}}=s)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>adm</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Spec</mtext><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{{\mathcal{O}}}_{\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}},\alpha}={\text{\rm Spec}\,}k[[z_{1},...,z_{b-4},t_{1},t_{2},...,t_{k},s]]/(t_{1}^{r_{1}}=t_{2}^{r_{2}}=...=t_{k}^{r_{k}}=s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This presentation is such that</p>
<table id="S2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{{\mathcal{O}}}_{[\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,b}/\mathfrak{S}_{b}],{\rm Br}(\alpha)}=k[[z_{1},...,z_{b-4},s]]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Br</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{{\mathcal{O}}}_{[\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,b}/\mathfrak{S}_{b}],{\rm Br}(\alpha)}=k[[z_{1},...,z_{b-4},s]]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and the obvious map <math id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{{\mathcal{O}}}_{[\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,b}/\mathfrak{S}_{b}],{\rm Br}(\alpha)}\longrightarrow\widehat{{\mathcal{O}}}_{\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}},\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Br</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>adm</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{{\mathcal{O}}}_{[\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,b}/\mathfrak{S}_{b}],{\rm Br}(\alpha)}\longrightarrow\widehat{{\mathcal{O}}}_{\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}},\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> gives the complete local description of the branch morphism</p>
<table id="S2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Br}^{\rm{adm}}{\colon}\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}\longrightarrow[\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,b}/\mathfrak{S}_{b}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Br</mi><mi>adm</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>adm</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Br}^{\rm{adm}}{\colon}\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}\longrightarrow[\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,b}/\mathfrak{S}_{b}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS10.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.10.2 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS10.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS10.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Above the veresal deformation space <math id="S2.SS10.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf Def}\,\alpha:={\text{\rm Spf}\,}{\widehat{{\mathcal{O}}}_{\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}},\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐃𝐞𝐟</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mtext>Spf</mtext><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>adm</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf Def}\,\alpha:={\text{\rm Spf}\,}{\widehat{{\mathcal{O}}}_{\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}},\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a versal family:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.Ex14.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="69.34" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-51.04313026049234px" version="1.1" viewBox="21.89 51.04 143.49 69.34" width="143.49"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 21.890292148529387 69.33872871615341) translate(0,3.46) translate(21.89,0)"><g transform="translate(-21.89,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.56em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.04em;font-size:10pt;" height="10" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="35.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex14.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{C\subset\mathcal{{\mathcal{C}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{C\subset\mathcal{{\mathcal{C}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 21.890292148529387 -0.27673578005007266 L 21.890292148529387 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(42.98,0) translate(0,9.15) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.56em;--ltx-fo-height:0.72em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.99" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.99)" width="7.69"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex14.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\widehat{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\widehat{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(82.31,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 21.890292148529387 -0.27673578005007266 L 82.31332329475188 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 82.31332329475188 -0.27673578005007266 L 82.31332329475188 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 9.76727185975768 -8.151343506501227 L 9.826115425714768 -8.167790990491387" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(11.76,0) translate(0,-28.89) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.14)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.53em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.05" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="7.28"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex14.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\varphi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\varphi}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(39.76,0) translate(0,-33.13)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -3.54 6.56" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -7.09 2.31" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 9.76727185975768 -8.151343506501227 L 39.7588683144588 -33.131904649556354" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 39.70004586208835 -33.11944763344057 L 39.7588683144588 -33.131904649556354" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(82.31,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.24em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.04em;font-size:10pt;" height="10" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="30.98"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex14.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{P}\subset\mathcal{{\mathcal{P}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{P}\subset\mathcal{{\mathcal{P}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 92.60326199170645 -8.151343506501227 L 92.58586439631763 -8.152230277139978" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(76.08,0) translate(0,-27.95) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-2.09)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.47em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="4.17" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="6.47"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex14.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(63.92,0) translate(0,-33.13)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 7.03 2.46" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 3.4 6.63" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 92.60326199170645 -8.151343506501227 L 63.92165801989285 -33.131904649556354" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 63.93905561528167 -33.131904649556354 L 63.92165801989285 -33.131904649556354" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(30.19,0) translate(0,-43.43) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.57em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="35.52"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex14.m1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{\bf Def}\,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐃𝐞𝐟</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{\bf Def}\,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS10.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Locally around the node <math id="S2.SS10.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in{P}\subset{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in{P}\subset{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS10.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> has local equation <math id="S2.SS10.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv=s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv=s</annotation></semantics></math>. At the nodes <math id="S2.SS10.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}\in C\subset{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}\in C\subset{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS10.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2,...,k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2,...,k</annotation></semantics></math>, the total space <math id="S2.SS10.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> has local equation <math id="S2.SS10.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}y_{i}=t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}y_{i}=t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. In these local coordinates, the admissible cover <math id="S2.SS10.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is locally given by <math id="S2.SS10.SSS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\mapsto x_{i}^{r_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\mapsto x_{i}^{r_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS10.SSS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\mapsto y_{i}^{r_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\mapsto y_{i}^{r_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, the equations <math id="S2.SS10.SSS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=t_{1}=...=t_{k}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=t_{1}=...=t_{k}=0</annotation></semantics></math> cuts out the divisor <math id="S2.SS10.SSS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS10.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.10.3 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS10.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS10.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This local description of the boundary allows us to understand intersection multiplicities of partial pencil families with boundary components. So let</p>
<table id="S2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha{\colon}{\mathcal{C}}\longrightarrow{\mathcal{P}}\longrightarrow S" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha{\colon}{\mathcal{C}}\longrightarrow{\mathcal{P}}\longrightarrow S</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS10.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">be a general family contained in <math id="S2.SS10.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, let <math id="S2.SS10.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}=L_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}=L_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS10.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,...,k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,...,k</annotation></semantics></math> be the glued sections mapping to a marked section of nodes <math id="S2.SS10.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf 0}\subset{\mathcal{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf 0}\subset{\mathcal{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where, around the section <math id="S2.SS10.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}=L_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}=L_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> the map <math id="S2.SS10.SSS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> has local degree <math id="S2.SS10.SSS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S2.SS10.SSS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>𝟎</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf 0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS10.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS10.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The admissibility condition at the nodes tells us that</p>
<table id="S2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(N_{L_{i}/{\mathcal{C}}_{L}}\otimes N_{R_{i}/{\mathcal{C}}_{R}})^{\otimes r_{i}}=\deg(N_{L_{j}/{\mathcal{C}}_{L}}\otimes N_{R_{j}/{\mathcal{C}}_{R}})^{\otimes r_{j}}=\deg(N_{{\bf 0}/{\mathcal{P}}_{L}}\otimes N_{{\bf 0}/{\mathcal{P}}_{R}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(N_{L_{i}/{\mathcal{C}}_{L}}\otimes N_{R_{i}/{\mathcal{C}}_{R}})^{\otimes r_{i}}=\deg(N_{L_{j}/{\mathcal{C}}_{L}}\otimes N_{R_{j}/{\mathcal{C}}_{R}})^{\otimes r_{j}}=\deg(N_{{\bf 0}/{\mathcal{P}}_{L}}\otimes N_{{\bf 0}/{\mathcal{P}}_{R}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS10.SSS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Here the <math id="S2.SS10.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\bullet}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\bullet}</annotation></semantics></math> denote normal bundles.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS10.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.10.4 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS10.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS10.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose furthermore that <math id="S2.SS10.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\longrightarrow\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>adm</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\longrightarrow\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}</annotation></semantics></math> comes from a family <math id="S2.SS10.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\longrightarrow\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\longrightarrow\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. that <math id="S2.SS10.SSS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\longrightarrow\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>adm</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\longrightarrow\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{\rm{adm}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the coarse space of a <span id="S2.SS10.SSS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">twisted</span> partial pencil. The family <math id="S2.SS10.SSS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\longrightarrow\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\longrightarrow\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}</annotation></semantics></math> will have intersection number</p>
<table id="S2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\cdot\Delta^{\prime}={\rm deg}\,(N_{{\bf 0}/{\mathcal{P}}_{L}}\otimes N_{{\bf 0}/{\mathcal{P}}_{R}})/lcm(r_{1},...,r_{k})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\cdot\Delta^{\prime}={\rm deg}\,(N_{{\bf 0}/{\mathcal{P}}_{L}}\otimes N_{{\bf 0}/{\mathcal{P}}_{R}})/lcm(r_{1},...,r_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS10.SSS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with the boundary divisor <math id="S2.SS10.SSS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\prime}\subset\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\prime}\subset\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}</annotation></semantics></math> in which it lies. (We assume that <math id="S2.SS10.SSS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\longrightarrow\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\longrightarrow\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}</annotation></semantics></math> does not have additional isolated intersections with <math id="S2.SS10.SSS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, in which case we must add these contributions appropriately.) This follows from the observation that the order of ramification of the branch map from the normalization</p>
<table id="S2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Br}^{\nu}{\colon}({\bf Def}\,\alpha)^{\nu}\longrightarrow{\text{\rm Spf}\,}{\widehat{{\mathcal{O}}}_{[\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,b}/\mathfrak{S}_{b}],{\rm Br}(\alpha)}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Br</mi><mi>ν</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐃𝐞𝐟</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ν</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mtext>Spf</mtext><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Br</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Br}^{\nu}{\colon}({\bf Def}\,\alpha)^{\nu}\longrightarrow{\text{\rm Spf}\,}{\widehat{{\mathcal{O}}}_{[\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,b}/\mathfrak{S}_{b}],{\rm Br}(\alpha)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS10.SSS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">is <math id="S2.SS10.SSS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="lcm(r_{1},...,r_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">lcm(r_{1},...,r_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS11" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">2.11 Admissible reduction.</h3>

<div id="S2.SS11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At this point, it will be convenient to indicate how to perform “admissible reduction” in some commonly encountered situations.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS11.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.11.1 Setup.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose we have a family of degree <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> simply-branched covers <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}{\colon}{\mathcal{C}}_{t}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}{\colon}{\mathcal{C}}_{t}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, with smooth total space <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, parametrized by <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{t}:={\text{\rm Spec}\,}k[[t]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mtext>Spec</mtext><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{t}:={\text{\rm Spec}\,}k[[t]]</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> disjoint multi-sections <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1},...\sigma_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1},...\sigma_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> of degrees <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{1},...,d_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{1},...,d_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, each of which in some local coordinates <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z,t)</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by an equation of the form <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{d_{i}}-t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{d_{i}}-t=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, suppose <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\cup_{i}\sigma_{i}=\alpha_{t}^{-1}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∪</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cup_{i}\sigma_{i}=\alpha_{t}^{-1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, note that <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{1}+...+d_{m}=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{1}+...+d_{m}=d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our task is to attach a constant cover <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{L}{\colon}C_{L}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{L}{\colon}C_{L}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to the family <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at the <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> points of the multi-section <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\cup_{i}\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∪</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cup_{i}\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, we would like <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the right side of a partial pencil.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">There are two obstacles currently preventing us from accomplishing this: 1) The points of attachment for <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> are experiencing nontrivial monodromy, and 2) the points of attachment are not remaining distinct when <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS11.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.11.2 Base change.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to kill monodromy, we first make an order <math id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l:={\rm lcm}(d_{1},...,d_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>lcm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l:={\rm lcm}(d_{1},...,d_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> base change <math id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=s^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=s^{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{s}{\colon}{\mathcal{C}}_{s}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}\times\Delta_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{s}{\colon}{\mathcal{C}}_{s}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}\times\Delta_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the base change family. Letting <math id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{i}:=l/d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{i}:=l/d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we immediately see that we now have <math id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> sections <math id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{1},...,\tau_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{1},...,\tau_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> of the family <math id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, these sections are naturally grouped according to which multi-section <math id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> they originally arose from. The first <math id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sections intersect at a point <math id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}\in C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}\in C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the next <math id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> intersect at a point <math id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{2}\in C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{2}\in C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and so on.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS11.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.11.3 Separating the sections <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now we must separate the sections <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> – this requires some care, since we still need to produce an admissible cover. We examine the local situation around each point <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For this, let <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X:={\text{\rm Spec}\,}k[[z,s]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mtext>Spec</mtext><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X:={\text{\rm Spec}\,}k[[z,s]]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y:={\text{\rm Spec}\,}k[[w,s]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mtext>Spec</mtext><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y:={\text{\rm Spec}\,}k[[w,s]]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{s}:={\text{\rm Spec}\,}k[[s]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mtext>Spec</mtext><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{s}:={\text{\rm Spec}\,}k[[s]]</annotation></semantics></math>, and let</p>
<table id="S2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\text{local}}:X\longrightarrow Y" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mtext>local</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\text{local}}:X\longrightarrow Y</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">be the degree <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>-morphism defined by <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=z^{d_{i}}-s^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=z^{d_{i}}-s^{l}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is a local model for the map <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> near the points <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We now blow up <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> along the ideal <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I:=(z,s^{l_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I:=(z,s^{l_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> along the ideal <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J:=(w,s^{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J:=(w,s^{l})</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, we set</p>
<table id="S2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}:={\text{\rm Proj}\,}k[[z,s]][U,V]/Uz-Vs^{l_{i}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Proj</mtext><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}:={\text{\rm Proj}\,}k[[z,s]][U,V]/Uz-Vs^{l_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\prime}:={\text{\rm Proj}\,}k[[w,s]][A,B]/Aw-Bs^{l}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Proj</mtext><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\prime}:={\text{\rm Proj}\,}k[[w,s]][A,B]/Aw-Bs^{l}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Then the following map of graded rings provides the “local admissible replacement” <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{\prime}_{\text{local}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mtext>local</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{\prime}_{\text{local}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s\mapsto s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s\mapsto s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w\mapsto z^{d_{i}}-s^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w\mapsto z^{d_{i}}-s^{l}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A\mapsto U^{d_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A\mapsto U^{d_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B\mapsto V^{d_{i}}-U^{d_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B\mapsto V^{d_{i}}-U^{d_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The reader may easily check that the local “kissing” condition is met for <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{\prime}_{\text{local}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mtext>local</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{\prime}_{\text{local}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, the local sections defined by <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z-\zeta_{j}s^{l_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z-\zeta_{j}s^{l_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are the <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{l_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{l_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>-th roots of unity, are separated in the blow up <math id="S2.SS11.SSS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rmk">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 2.8</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that the ideal <math id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> is not the inverse image of the ideal <math id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>. In fact, an admissible cover with ramification occurring above a node is never a flat map. Therefore, the ideal <math id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> could not have been the inverse image of <math id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS11.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.11.4 Triple ramification.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS11.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now suppose <math id="S2.SS11.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a family of covers aquiring a triple ramification point <math id="S2.SS11.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in C_{0}\subset{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in C_{0}\subset{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the reader may check that the admissible reduction of this family requires at least an order two base change.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rmk">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 2.9</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Triple ramification is a divisorial phenomenon. Since we will be using many one parameter families, it will be a nuisance to have to perform admissible reduction each time it occurs. This is why we eventually pass to the space <math id="S2.Thmthm9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS12" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">2.12 Constructions of partial pencils.</h3>

<div id="S2.SS12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We will frequently use one particular construction of partial pencil families. The basic idea will be introduced in this section.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS12.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.12.1 Basic Setup.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi{\colon}{\bf F}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi{\colon}{\bf F}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth surface fibered over <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> the projection. Let <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> be a smooth curve on <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}</annotation></semantics></math>, and denote the degree of <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi{\colon}C\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi{\colon}C\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. We let <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> denote the genus of <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we mark a general point <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf 0}\in{\bf P}^{1}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf 0}\in{\bf P}^{1}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, label the corresponding fiber <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\subset{\bf F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>𝐅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\subset{\bf F}</annotation></semantics></math>, and mark <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> distinct points <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},...,p_{d}\subset F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},...,p_{d}\subset F</annotation></semantics></math>. We choose a pencil</p>
<table id="S2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\subset|{\mathcal{O}}_{{\bf F}}(C)|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>𝐅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\subset|{\mathcal{O}}_{{\bf F}}(C)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">in the linear system of <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> such that the base locus <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> contains the set <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{1},...,p_{d}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{1},...,p_{d}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p{\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p{\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the total space of the pencil, i.e. <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=Bl_{B}{\bf F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐅</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=Bl_{B}{\bf F}</annotation></semantics></math> is the blow up of <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}</annotation></semantics></math> along <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the pencil is forced to be constant on the marked fiber <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that at some point, which we take as <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\infty\in{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\infty\in{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the curve <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{-1}(\infty)=C^{\prime}\cup F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∪</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{-1}(\infty)=C^{\prime}\cup F</annotation></semantics></math> becomes reducible.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We make the following assumption, which will be true in all cases we encounter: <span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">We assume that <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is at-worst-nodal and meets <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> trasversely at smooth points.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Our task is to realize the pencil <math id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> as the right side of a partial pencil family.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS12.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.12.2 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The induced map <math id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{R}{\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{s}\times{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{R}{\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{s}\times{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite everywhere except over the point <math id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,\infty)\in{\bf P}^{1}_{s}\times{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,\infty)\in{\bf P}^{1}_{s}\times{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the preimage is the curve <math id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>. If we let <math id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{{\bf P}^{1}_{s}\times{\bf P}^{1}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{{\bf P}^{1}_{s}\times{\bf P}^{1}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the blow up at <math id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that <math id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> factors through <math id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{{\bf P}^{1}_{s}\times{\bf P}^{1}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{{\bf P}^{1}_{s}\times{\bf P}^{1}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
<table id="S2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{R}{\colon}X\longrightarrow\widetilde{{\bf P}^{1}_{s}\times{\bf P}^{1}_{t}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{R}{\colon}X\longrightarrow\widetilde{{\bf P}^{1}_{s}\times{\bf P}^{1}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is finite and flat.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The section <math id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,t){\colon}{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\longrightarrow\widetilde{{\bf P}^{1}_{s}\times{\bf P}^{1}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,t){\colon}{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\longrightarrow\widetilde{{\bf P}^{1}_{s}\times{\bf P}^{1}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> together with the sections of <math id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p{\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p{\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> induced by the basepoints <math id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> provide the data of a family of marked admissible covers, as in section <a href="#S2.SS9.SSS1" title="2.9.1 ‣ 2.9 Partial pencil families. ‣ 2 Compactifications. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.9.1</span></a>. The family <math id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> can now be attached (perhaps after a base change) to a constant family of covers on a constant left hand side <math id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{L}{\colon}C_{L}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{L}{\colon}C_{L}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. This produces a partial pencil family, which we will refer to simply by <math id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS12.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.12.3 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The family <math id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> clearly lies entirely within a boundary divisor <math id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>. The admissible covers in <math id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> originally associated to the point <math id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> before base change, provide intersections with another boundary divisor, which we refer to by <math id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\rm split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>split</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\rm split}</annotation></semantics></math>. (Indeed, the target of these admissible covers splits off a third component.)</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.10</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Split Fiber)<span id="S2.Thmthm10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Maintain the notation and setting above. The admissible covers in the partial pencil family <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to the point <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> are called <span id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">split fibers</span>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">(This language is used to remind the reader that the component <math id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is “splitting off”, creating an intersection with a new higher boundary divisor.)</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="/html/1508.06016/assets/SplitFiber1.svg" id="S2.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" width="238" height="78"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>Acquiring a split fiber.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS12.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.12.4 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS12.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We will be interested in pencils satisfying the following genericity conditions:</p>
<ol id="S2.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The curves parametrized by <math id="S2.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are at-worst-nodal.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The split fiber <math id="S2.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is simply branched under the map <math id="S2.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{R}{\colon}X\longrightarrow\widetilde{{\bf P}^{1}_{s}\times{\bf P}^{1}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{R}{\colon}X\longrightarrow\widetilde{{\bf P}^{1}_{s}\times{\bf P}^{1}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The residual curve <math id="S2.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in the split fiber is at-worst-nodal and intersects <math id="S2.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S2.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> distinct points.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">These conditions have to be checked in every situation. However, this is usually a standard application of Bertini’s theorem and dimension counts, so we usually omit this check.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rmk">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 2.11</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We should mention that there are essentially two ways of producing one parameter families of branched covers. The first and conceptually simpler way is by “varying the branch points”. Effectively, this means to start with a curve <math id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset[\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,b}/\mathfrak{S}_{b}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset[\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,b}/\mathfrak{S}_{b}]</annotation></semantics></math>, and then lift it to Hurwitz space via the finite branch morphism. The task of determining how many times the family meets various boundary components involves very difficult combinatorics, which we choose to avoid at all costs. See <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx17" title="" class="ltx_ref">EEHS91</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm11.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm11.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The other approach is to vary covers as divisors on fibered surfaces or as complete intersections in higher dimensional varieties. This is the approach we have taken. It is much easier to understand how these families intersect various boundary components of Hurwitz space. The drawback is that the constructions are ad hoc, and do not “cover generic moduli” once the degree <math id="S2.Thmthm11.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is large.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS12.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.12.5 Variation on the basic construction I.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now modify the construction above by imposing nonreduced base points in the pencil <math id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\subset|{\mathcal{O}}_{{\bf F}}(C)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>𝐅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\subset|{\mathcal{O}}_{{\bf F}}(C)|</annotation></semantics></math>. Maintaining the notation and setting above, let <math id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{1},p_{2},...,p_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{1},p_{2},...,p_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a set of distinct points in <math id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;d</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the closed subscheme <math id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\subset F\subset{\bf F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>𝐅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\subset F\subset{\bf F}</annotation></semantics></math> isomorphic to <math id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\text{\rm Spec}\,}k[\epsilon]/(\epsilon^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Spec</mtext><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\text{\rm Spec}\,}k[\epsilon]/(\epsilon^{m})</annotation></semantics></math> supported on the point <math id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=d-k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=d-k-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As before, pick a pencil <math id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\subset|{\mathcal{O}}_{{\bf F}}(C)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>𝐅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\subset|{\mathcal{O}}_{{\bf F}}(C)|</annotation></semantics></math> containing the scheme <math id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\cup p_{2}\cup...\cup p_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\cup p_{2}\cup...\cup p_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> in its base locus <math id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>; choose the pencil to be general among such pencils. We assume that the pencil <math id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> generically parameterizes smooth curves having order <math id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> ramification at the point <math id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The point <math id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> will denote the split fiber, where the component <math id="S2.SS12.SSS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> splits off.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS12.SSS6" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.12.6 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is one more element of the pencil <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> which is very important for our purposes. The total space <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=Bl_{B}{\bf F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐅</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=Bl_{B}{\bf F}</annotation></semantics></math> has a unique <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math> singularity <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> coming from blowing up the nonreduced scheme <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>. As before, let <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p{\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p{\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the total family of the pencil, and assume that the singular point <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in X</annotation></semantics></math> occurs over the point <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\in{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\in{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the curve <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}:=p^{-1}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}:=p^{-1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math> is a singular curve in <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, possessing a node at the point <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. We assume <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> has no singularities outside of the node <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The point <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}\in C_{0}\subset{\bf F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>𝐅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}\in C_{0}\subset{\bf F}</annotation></semantics></math> is then a “ramified node”; one of the branches is tangent to order <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-1</annotation></semantics></math> along the fiber <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, while the other branch meets <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> transversely. Let <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1},...,s_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1},...,s_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the sections of <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p{\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p{\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to the reduced base points points <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},...,p_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},...,p_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Observe that <math id="S2.SS12.SSS6.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS12.SSS7" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.12.7 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now we produce the admissible reduction of the total family <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly, the singular point <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is problematic, as it lies on the section <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, so we desingularize the <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math> singularity <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in X</annotation></semantics></math>, to obtain a new family <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}{\colon}\widetilde{X}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}{\colon}\widetilde{X}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with fiber <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}^{-1}(0)=\widetilde{C}_{0}\cup E_{1}\cup...\cup E_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}^{-1}(0)=\widetilde{C}_{0}\cup E_{1}\cup...\cup E_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalization of <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are the exceptional divisors of the standard desingularization of an <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math> singularity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The normalization <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> intersects the exceptional curves <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we may assume that the section <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{s}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{s}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> passes through <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> transversely at a point <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. All other sections <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> are unaffected by the blow up.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next contract all exceptional curves <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, introducing an <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{m-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{m-2}</annotation></semantics></math> singular point <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. (We continue to use “<math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>” for this remaining exceptional divisor.) Finally we blow up the <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k-1</annotation></semantics></math> smooth points <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\cap\widetilde{C}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\cap\widetilde{C}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. In summary, we arrive at a family <math id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}{\colon}\overline{X}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}{\colon}\overline{X}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the following properties:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS7.p4" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S2.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="S2.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> disjoint sections <math id="S2.I5.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> all contained in the smooth locus of the map <math id="S2.I5.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The fiber <math id="S2.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}^{-1}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}^{-1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S2.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}_{0}\cup E_{1}\cup P_{2}\cup...\cup P_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}_{0}\cup E_{1}\cup P_{2}\cup...\cup P_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. These components intersect transversally as follows: <math id="S2.I5.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I5.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> intersect at two points <math id="S2.I5.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I5.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.I5.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I5.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> intersect at one point. All other components are mutually disjoint.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S2.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> has two special points <math id="S2.I5.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=\bar{s}_{1}\cap E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=\bar{s}_{1}\cap E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I5.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="S2.I5.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{m-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{m-2}</annotation></semantics></math> singularity of <math id="S2.I5.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. The point <math id="S2.I5.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth point of <math id="S2.I5.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S2.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is a distinguished pencil of degree <math id="S2.I5.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> on the component <math id="S2.I5.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> spanned by the divisors <math id="S2.I5.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\cdot a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\cdot a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I5.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m-1)\cdot x+b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m-1)\cdot x+b</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, there are distinguished pencils of degree one on each <math id="S2.I5.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> spanned by the points <math id="S2.I5.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}_{i}\cap P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}_{i}\cap P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I5.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}_{0}\cap P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}_{0}\cap P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I5.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="S2.I5.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I5.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have: <math id="S2.I5.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}_{1}^{2}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}_{1}^{2}=-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS12.SSS8" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.12.8 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS12.SSS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After dealing with the split fiber <math id="S2.SS12.SSS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> in the usual way, (and after base changes from any necessary admissible reduction) we may attach a fixed cover <math id="S2.SS12.SSS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{L}{\colon}C_{L}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{L}{\colon}C_{L}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> with ramification profile <math id="S2.SS12.SSS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m+1+...+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m+1+...+1</annotation></semantics></math> above <math id="S2.SS12.SSS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\in{\bf P}^{1}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\in{\bf P}^{1}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> along the sections <math id="S2.SS12.SSS8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bar{s}_{1},...,\bar{s}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bar{s}_{1},...,\bar{s}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS12.SSS8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> denote the resulting partial pencil family. Then <math id="S2.SS12.SSS8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> has the following properties which are most important for us:</p>
<ol id="S2.I6" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is completely contained in a ramified boundary divisor <math id="S2.I6.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> intersects the standard boundary divisors <math id="S2.I6.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\rm irr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>irr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\rm irr}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.I6.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.I6.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> nonnegatively.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S2.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I6.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> intersects an unramified boundary divisor <math id="S2.I6.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\rm split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>split</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\rm split}</annotation></semantics></math>. This corresponds to the split fiber <math id="S2.I6.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> in the original pencil <math id="S2.I6.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I6.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S2.I6.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I6.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I6.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> intersects one other higher boundary divisor <math id="S2.I6.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\rm ram}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ram</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\rm ram}</annotation></semantics></math>, corresponding to the element <math id="S2.I6.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> from the original pencil. The ramification index <math id="S2.I6.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\Delta_{\rm ram})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ram</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\Delta_{\rm ram})</annotation></semantics></math> is one less than the ramification index <math id="S2.I6.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.12</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Reduced Ramification fibers)<span id="S2.Thmthm12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In any partial pencil family <math id="S2.Thmthm12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> constructed as above, we call the fibers corresponding to <math id="S2.Thmthm12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S2.Thmthm12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">reduced ramification fibers</span>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="/html/1508.06016/assets/ReducedandSplit.svg" id="S2.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" width="238" height="215"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>A picture of the initial pencil <math id="S2.F2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p{\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p{\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> acquiring a split fiber at <math id="S2.F2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and a reduced ramification fiber at <math id="S2.F2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>. The “<math id="S2.F2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>” indicates an <math id="S2.F2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> singularity on <math id="S2.F2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> in this example.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S2.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="/html/1508.06016/assets/ramifiedpartialpencil.svg" id="S2.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" width="238" height="172"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>A schematic picture of a partial pencil acquiring a split fiber and ramification reduction.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS12.SSS9" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.12.9 Variation on the basic construction II.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS12.SSS9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When constructing families of pentagonal curves, we will find ourselves in a situation not yet encountered in the previous two settings. This variation will not be needed in order to prove <a href="#Thmmaintheorem1" title="Theorem A (Independence of the boundary). ‣ 0.2 Outline and main results. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>, so the reader may skip ahead and come back when needed.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS9.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We return to the general setting: <math id="S2.SS12.SSS9.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi{\colon}{\bf F}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi{\colon}{\bf F}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is a fibered surface and <math id="S2.SS12.SSS9.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\mathcal{O}}_{{\bf F}}(C)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>𝐅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\mathcal{O}}_{{\bf F}}(C)|</annotation></semantics></math> an appropriate degree <math id="S2.SS12.SSS9.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, genus <math id="S2.SS12.SSS9.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> linear system. We now pick a general pencil <math id="S2.SS12.SSS9.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}_{t}\subset|{\mathcal{O}}_{{\bf F}}(C)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>𝐅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}_{t}\subset|{\mathcal{O}}_{{\bf F}}(C)|</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="S2.SS12.SSS9.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">without any assumption on its base locus.</span> Our goal is to make this pencil the right side of a partial pencil.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS12.SSS10" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.12.10 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS12.SSS10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We assume that the pencil <math id="S2.SS12.SSS10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, when restricted to the fiber curve <math id="S2.SS12.SSS10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:=\pi^{-1}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:=\pi^{-1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math> is basepoint free, and that the induced branched cover <math id="S2.SS12.SSS10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is simply branched except possible at one point <math id="S2.SS12.SSS10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0\in P^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0\in P^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> where the branching profile is <math id="S2.SS12.SSS10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{1},...,m_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{1},...,m_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS12.SSS10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}m_{i}=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}m_{i}=d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS12.SSS11" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.12.11 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p{\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p{\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the total space of the pencil, where <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is the blow up of <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}</annotation></semantics></math> along the base locus of the pencil. Then <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p,\pi){\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\times{\bf P}^{1}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p,\pi){\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\times{\bf P}^{1}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite, degree <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> map, and the curve <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is the preimage of the line <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\times\{s=0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\times\{s=0\}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-fold multi-section of the morphism <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Of course we cannot glue a fixed family to the family <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> along the multi-section <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> for two reasons: <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1)</annotation></semantics></math> the monodromy of the projection <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> interchanges the <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> points of attachment, and <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2)</annotation></semantics></math> the ramification points of this projection pose an obvious obstruction to glueing.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To overcome the first issue, we make the base change <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta{\colon}D\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta{\colon}D\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d!</annotation></semantics></math> which kills all monodromy of the cover <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this way we obtain the base changed family <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{D}{\colon}X_{D}\longrightarrow D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{D}{\colon}X_{D}\longrightarrow D</annotation></semantics></math> which now has <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> sections <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1},...,\sigma_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1},...,\sigma_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Here <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{D}:=X\times_{{\bf P}^{1}_{t}}D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></msub><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{D}:=X\times_{{\bf P}^{1}_{t}}D</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The local nature of the map <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is summarized as follows:</p>
<ol id="S2.I7" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each branch point <math id="S2.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.I7.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> not equal to <math id="S2.I7.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, there are <math id="S2.I7.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d!/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d!/2</annotation></semantics></math> preimages in <math id="S2.I7.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> which, as a set, we denote by <math id="S2.I7.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{z}\subset D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{z}\subset D</annotation></semantics></math>. Each point in <math id="S2.I7.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> experiences <math id="S2.I7.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2:1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2:1</annotation></semantics></math> branching under the map <math id="S2.I7.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Above the point <math id="S2.I7.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\in{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\in{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, there are <math id="S2.I7.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d!/lcm(m_{1},...,m_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d!/lcm(m_{1},...,m_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> preimages, which we denote by <math id="S2.I7.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{0}\subset{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{0}\subset{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Every point in <math id="S2.I7.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> experiences <math id="S2.I7.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="lcm(m_{1},...,m_{k}):1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">lcm(m_{1},...,m_{k}):1</annotation></semantics></math> branching under the map <math id="S2.I7.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The sections <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are not disjoint in the surface <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> – they meet in two ways:</p>
<ol id="S2.I8" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I8.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I8.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> meet above a point <math id="S2.I8.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in A_{z}\subset D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in A_{z}\subset D</annotation></semantics></math> for some set <math id="S2.I8.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> as defined above.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I8.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I8.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> meet above a point <math id="S2.I8.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in B_{0}\subset D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in B_{0}\subset D</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In the first setting, the sections <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> meet transversely above <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in D</annotation></semantics></math>, and the remaining sections remain disjoint. In the latter case, <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> will meet with tangency order <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="lcm(m_{1},...,m_{k})/m_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">lcm(m_{1},...,m_{k})/m_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> depending on the pair of sections. This is exactly the setting achieved when performing admissible reduction in section <a href="#S2.SS11" title="2.11 Admissible reduction. ‣ 2 Compactifications. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.11</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p7.1" class="ltx_p">By blowing up these intersections appropriately, as described in section <a href="#S2.SS11" title="2.11 Admissible reduction. ‣ 2 Compactifications. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.11</span></a>, we obtain a partial pencil family <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained by attaching an unchanging cover on the left. The family <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is completely contained in a boundary divisor <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>. It interacts with two other boundary divisors: <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{{\rm simple}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>simple</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{{\rm simple}}</annotation></semantics></math> at the points in <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{{m_{1},...,m_{k}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{{m_{1},...,m_{k}}}</annotation></semantics></math> at the points in <math id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.13</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The resulting partial pencil <math id="S2.Thmthm13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> intersects <math id="S2.Thmthm13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{{\rm simple}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>simple</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{{\rm simple}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.Thmthm13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{{m_{1},...,m_{k}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{{m_{1},...,m_{k}}}</annotation></semantics></math> transversely at the points in <math id="S2.Thmthm13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.Thmthm13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS11.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS11.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">This follows easily from the local coordinates description of the versal deformation spaces found in section <a href="#S2.SS10" title="2.10 Intersection multiplicities. ‣ 2 Compactifications. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.10</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS13" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">2.13 Some explicit partial pencils.</h3>

<div id="S2.SS13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now construct some useful partial pencil families.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS13.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.13.1 Rational partial pencils.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the linear system of <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,d)</annotation></semantics></math> curves on the surface <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}={\bf P}^{1}\times{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}={\bf P}^{1}\times{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and pick a <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-tuple of distinct points <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=\{p_{1},...,p_{d}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\{p_{1},...,p_{d}\}</annotation></semantics></math> lying entirely in a <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,0)</annotation></semantics></math> ruling curve <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider a general linear pencil <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\subset|(1,d)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\subset|(1,d)|</annotation></semantics></math> whose base locus <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> contains <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The total space <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> of the pencil</p>
<table id="S2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\colon X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\colon X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">then has the following features:</p>
<ul id="S2.I9" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S2.I9.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I9.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I9.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The split fiber <math id="S2.I9.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S2.I9.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\cup R_{1}\cup...\cup R_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\cup R_{1}\cup...\cup R_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S2.I9.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are disjoint <math id="S2.I9.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> rulings.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I9.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I9.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I9.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There are <math id="S2.I9.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> fibers of the form <math id="S2.I9.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}\cup B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}\cup B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S2.I9.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="S2.I9.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> lines and <math id="S2.I9.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are smooth <math id="S2.I9.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,d-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,d-1)</annotation></semantics></math> curves.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I9.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I9.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I9.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The section <math id="S2.I9.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.I9.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>
corresponding to the basepoint <math id="S2.I9.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> obeys <math id="S2.I9.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{2}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{2}=-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The curves <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> can be contracted to create a family <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{p}\longrightarrow\overline{X}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{p}\longrightarrow\overline{X}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> – we continue to use <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the transformed section. Since the <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> did not pass through the points <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we still have <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{2}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{2}=-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We may attach a fixed cover along the sections <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain a partial pencil. Away from <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, we only obtain intersections with enumeratively relevant divisors: triple ramification, <math id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2,2)</annotation></semantics></math>-ramification, and simple nodes will appear. Since these partial pencils are obtained by varying rational curves, we will call them <span id="S2.SS13.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">rational partial pencils</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS13.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.13.2 Hyperelliptic families.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Every hyperelliptic curve <math id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> of genus <math id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> can be embedded in the Hirzebruch surface <math id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}:={\bf F}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}:={\bf F}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> as a curve in the linear system <math id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|2\tau+f|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|2\tau+f|</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is the section class with <math id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{2}=h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{2}=h</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is the fiber class.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By fixing two general points <math id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=\{p_{1},p_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\{p_{1},p_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math> in a ruling line <math id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\subset{\bf F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>𝐅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\subset{\bf F}</annotation></semantics></math> to be lie the base locus of a pencil <math id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\subset|2\tau+f|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\subset|2\tau+f|</annotation></semantics></math> we obtain the family</p>
<table id="S2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p{\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p{\colon}X\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is the total space of the pencil.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The family <math id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> has a split fiber <math id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\cup C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∪</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\cup C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a hyperelliptic curve of genus <math id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h-1</annotation></semantics></math>. This family has two sections <math id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1},\sigma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1},\sigma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> along which we may attach more components to create partial pencils. We call partial pencil families constructed in this way <span id="S2.SS13.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">hyperelliptic partial pencils</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS13.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.13.3 Ramification reducing families.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Start with a pencil <math id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\subset|(1,d)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\subset|(1,d)|</annotation></semantics></math> of bidegree <math id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,d)</annotation></semantics></math> curves on <math id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}:={\bf P}^{1}\times{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}:={\bf P}^{1}\times{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> containing a scheme <math id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z={\text{\rm Spec}\,}k[\epsilon]/(\epsilon^{d})\subset F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Spec</mtext><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z={\text{\rm Spec}\,}k[\epsilon]/(\epsilon^{d})\subset F</annotation></semantics></math> in its base locus. (As usual, we assume our pencil is generic among those satisfying this constraint.)</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Then, as in <a href="#S2.SS12.SSS5" title="2.12.5 Variation on the basic construction I. ‣ 2.12 Constructions of partial pencils. ‣ 2 Compactifications. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">subsubsection 2.12.5</span></a>, there is one distinguished element in the resulting partial pencil <math id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to a ramification reducing fiber. This pencil <math id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> lies entirely within a unique boundary divisor <math id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> and intersects the ramification reduction <math id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{{\rm ram}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ram</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{{\rm ram}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We need a slight generalization of the pencil above. In particular we will need to fix a <span id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">different</span> fiber <math id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and create a partial pencil with two places to attach the rest of an admissible cover. Of course, in order for the fiber <math id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to create a family of gluing sections, we must make an appropriate base change as in section <a href="#S2.SS12.SSS9" title="2.12.9 Variation on the basic construction II. ‣ 2.12 Constructions of partial pencils. ‣ 2 Compactifications. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.12.9</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The resulting partial pencil <math id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> lives in <span id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">two</span> boundary divisors: <math id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{{\rm unram}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>unram</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{{\rm unram}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, it intersects <math id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{{\rm ram}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ram</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{{\rm ram}}</annotation></semantics></math> as before, but also intersects a divisor <math id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{{\rm simple}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>simple</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{{\rm simple}}</annotation></semantics></math>, corresponding to the points “<math id="S2.SS13.SSS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{z}</annotation></semantics></math>” as in section <a href="#S2.SS12.SSS9" title="2.12.9 Variation on the basic construction II. ‣ 2.12 Constructions of partial pencils. ‣ 2 Compactifications. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.12.9</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS14" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">2.14 Independence of the boundary.</h3>

<div id="S2.SS14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At this point, we have all necessary ingredients to prove <a href="#Thmmaintheorem1" title="Theorem A (Independence of the boundary). ‣ 0.2 Outline and main results. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS14.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.14.1 Independence of the boundary of <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First we need to understand the boundary of the partial compactification <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2.14</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.Thmthm14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{T}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.Thmthm14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, <math id="S2.Thmthm14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the boundary divisors are independent in <math id="S2.Thmthm14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Pic}_{{\bf Q}}\,\widetilde{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Pic}_{{\bf Q}}\,\widetilde{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> be the boundary divisor in <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}</annotation></semantics></math> generically parametrizing covers</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha{\colon}C_{1}\cup C_{2}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha{\colon}C_{1}\cup C_{2}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(C_{1})=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(C_{1})=i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg\alpha|_{C_{1}}=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg\alpha|_{C_{1}}=j</annotation></semantics></math>. (Note: <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i,j}=\delta_{g-i,d-j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i,j}=\delta_{g-i,d-j}</annotation></semantics></math>.) Furthermore, let <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\rm irr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>irr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\rm irr}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the boundary divisor generically parameterizing covers <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha{\colon}C\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha{\colon}C\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is irreducible and nodal.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Begin with any relation:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0=a\cdot{\mathsf{T}}+b\cdot{\mathsf{D}}+c\cdot\delta_{\rm irr}+\sum c_{i,j}\cdot\delta_{i,j}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝖳</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝖣</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>irr</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0=a\cdot{\mathsf{T}}+b\cdot{\mathsf{D}}+c\cdot\delta_{\rm irr}+\sum c_{i,j}\cdot\delta_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We use test families to express the coefficients <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> as linear combinations of <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. The divisor classes <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\rm irr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>irr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\rm irr}</annotation></semantics></math> are known to be independent <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx16" title="" class="ltx_ref">DP15</a>]</cite>[Proposition 2.15].</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.15</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The coefficients <math id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> are linear combinations of <math id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS1.2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> be the family of covers obtained by varying a <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,k)</annotation></semantics></math> curve in a pencil on <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}\times{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}\times{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and attaching a fixed general genus <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, degree <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d-k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d-k</annotation></semantics></math> cover <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> at a base point of the pencil.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then the family <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> interacts nontrivially with the divisors <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0,k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0,k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0,k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0,1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">In addition to the families <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> consider the following families:</span></p>
<ol id="S2.I10" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I10.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S2.I10.i1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> 
<div id="S2.I10.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I10.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Begin with a general pencil <math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> of hyperelliptic genus <math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> curves on <math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> and attach a fixed general degree <math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d-2</annotation></semantics></math> genus <math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> cover <math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> at a base point of the pencil. <math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> has nontrivial intersection with <math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0,d-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0,d-2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\rm irr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>irr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\rm irr}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I10.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S2.I10.ix1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> 
<div id="S2.I10.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I10.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Begin with a pencil <math id="S2.I10.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> of trigonal genus <math id="S2.I10.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> covers on a Hirzebruch surface, and attach an unchanging degree <math id="S2.I10.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d-3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d-3</annotation></semantics></math> rational cover <math id="S2.I10.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> at a base point. <math id="S2.I10.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> has nontrivial intersection with <math id="S2.I10.ix1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0,d-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0,d-3}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.I10.ix1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.I10.ix1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\rm irr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>irr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\rm irr}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.I10.ix1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">The families <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> provide enough relations to conclude <a href="#S2.Thmthm15" title="Lemma 2.15. ‣ Proof. ‣ 2.14.1 Independence of the boundary of 
            
              
                
                
                  ~
                  H
                
                
                  
                    
                    
                    
                  
                  
                    d
                    ,
                    g
                  
                
              
            
          . ‣ 2.14 Independence of the boundary. ‣ 2 Compactifications. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.15</span></a> for coefficients of the form <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0,k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we argue that knowing <a href="#S2.Thmthm15" title="Lemma 2.15. ‣ Proof. ‣ 2.14.1 Independence of the boundary of 
            
              
                
                
                  ~
                  H
                
                
                  
                    
                    
                    
                  
                  
                    d
                    ,
                    g
                  
                
              
            
          . ‣ 2.14 Independence of the boundary. ‣ 2 Compactifications. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.15</span></a> for the coefficients <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0,k}</annotation></semantics></math> allows one to deduce it for all coefficients <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, suppose <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then it must follow that <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. (The genus <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> component must map with degree <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the following family:</span></p>
<ol id="S2.I11" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I11.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S2.I11.i1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> 
<div id="S2.I11.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I11.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Begin with a general pencil <math id="S2.I11.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> of hyperelliptic curves of genus <math id="S2.I11.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> on the Hirzebruch surface <math id="S2.I11.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. At one base point, attach an unchanging genus <math id="S2.I11.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g-i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g-i</annotation></semantics></math> cover <math id="S2.I11.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S2.I11.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d-j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d-j</annotation></semantics></math>. Choose a second base point (which is not the hyperelliptic conjugate to the first), and attach a second unchanging genus <math id="S2.I11.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> cover <math id="S2.I11.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S2.I11.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j-2</annotation></semantics></math>. (If <math id="S2.I11.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=2</annotation></semantics></math>, simply omit <math id="S2.I11.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.)</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">The family <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> only interacts nontrivially with <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\rm irr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>irr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\rm irr}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{0,j-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{0,j-2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The relations obtained from the test families of type <math id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> allow us to finally conclude <a href="#S2.Thmthm15" title="Lemma 2.15. ‣ Proof. ‣ 2.14.1 Independence of the boundary of 
            
              
                
                
                  ~
                  H
                
                
                  
                    
                    
                    
                  
                  
                    d
                    ,
                    g
                  
                
              
            
          . ‣ 2.14 Independence of the boundary. ‣ 2 Compactifications. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.15</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS14.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.14.2 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS14.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let’s return to the proof of <a href="#Thmmaintheorem1" title="Theorem A (Independence of the boundary). ‣ 0.2 Outline and main results. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>. We use the method of test families. Begin with a dependence relation in <math id="S2.SS14.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Pic}_{{\bf Q}}\,\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Pic}_{{\bf Q}}\,\overline{{\mathcal{H}}}_{d,g}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S2.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0=\sum_{\Delta}c(\Delta)\cdot\Delta" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></munder><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0=\sum_{\Delta}c(\Delta)\cdot\Delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let us rewrite the dependence relation as:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a{\mathsf{T}}+b\Delta_{\rm irr}+c{\mathsf{D}}+\sum_{\Delta^{\prime}\text{\,\, enum. relevant.}}c(\Delta^{\prime})\cdot\Delta^{\prime}+\sum_{\Delta}c(\Delta)\cdot\Delta=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖳</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>irr</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖣</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> enum. relevant.</mtext></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></munder><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a{\mathsf{T}}+b\Delta_{\rm irr}+c{\mathsf{D}}+\sum_{\Delta^{\prime}\text{\,\, enum. relevant.}}c(\Delta^{\prime})\cdot\Delta^{\prime}+\sum_{\Delta}c(\Delta)\cdot\Delta=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where the first sum is over all enumeratively relevant divisors <span id="S2.SS14.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">other than</span> <math id="S2.SS14.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{T}},{\mathsf{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖣</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{T}},{\mathsf{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS14.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\rm irr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>irr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\rm irr}</annotation></semantics></math>. We will refer to the coefficients <math id="S2.SS14.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS14.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS14.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS14.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> as the <span id="S2.SS14.SSS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">enumeratively relevant</span> coefficients.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS14.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">2.14.3 </h4>

<div id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The first claim we make is</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2.16</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The coefficients <math id="S2.Thmthm16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math> are linear combinations of enumeratively relevant coefficients.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Before proving <a href="#S2.Thmthm16" title="Proposition 2.16. ‣ 2.14.3 ‣ 2.14 Independence of the boundary. ‣ 2 Compactifications. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.16</span></a>, we will need a definition.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.17</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm17.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S2.Thmthm17.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">excess</span>, <math id="S2.Thmthm17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm ex}(\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ex</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm ex}(\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math>, of a boundary divisor <math id="S2.Thmthm17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is the number</p>
<table id="S2.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm ex}(\Delta):=\min\Big\{r(\Delta)+\sum_{v\,\,\textrm{L-vertex}}g_{v},\,\,r(\Delta)+\sum_{v\,\,\textrm{R-vertex}}g_{v}\Big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ex</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>L-vertex</mtext></mrow></munder><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.507em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>R-vertex</mtext></mrow></munder><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm ex}(\Delta):=\min\Big\{r(\Delta)+\sum_{v\,\,\textrm{L-vertex}}g_{v},\,\,r(\Delta)+\sum_{v\,\,\textrm{R-vertex}}g_{v}\Big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Observe that the divisors <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm ex}(\Delta)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ex</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm ex}(\Delta)=0</annotation></semantics></math> are precisely those which are unramified and have only rational components on one side.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm18" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.18</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm18.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm18.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm18.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S2.Thmthm18.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm ex}(\Delta)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ex</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm ex}(\Delta)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S2.Thmthm18.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math> is a linear combination of the enumeratively relevant coefficients.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Pick a rational vertex <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\Gamma_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\Gamma_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> which has degree <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{v}\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{v}\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Vary <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in a rational partial pencil as in <a href="#S2.SS13.SSS1" title="2.13.1 Rational partial pencils. ‣ 2.13 Some explicit partial pencils. ‣ 2 Compactifications. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">subsubsection 2.13.1</span></a>. The resulting partial pencil test family <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> has negative intersection with <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> and otherwise only interacts with enumeratively relevant boundary divisors. Therefore, we obtain a relation relating <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math> with enumeratively relevant coefficients, which is what we wanted to show.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm19" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.19</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm19.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm19.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm19.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="S2.Thmthm19.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm ex}(\Delta)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ex</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm ex}(\Delta)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S2.Thmthm19.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math> is a linear combination of the enumeratively relevant coefficients and various <math id="S2.Thmthm19.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.Thmthm19.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm ex}(\Delta_{i})&lt;{\rm ex}(\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ex</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>ex</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm ex}(\Delta_{i})&lt;{\rm ex}(\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">If the divisor <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is unramified, pick a vertex <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\Gamma_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\Gamma_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> of genus <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{v}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{v}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> on the side with smaller total sum of genera. Suppose the dual graph, locally around <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, has the following form:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
