<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we vary the genus <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> hyperelliptic curve corresponding to <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in a pencil of <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|2\tau+f|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|2\tau+f|</annotation></semantics></math> curves on <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}_{g_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}_{g_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <span id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_slanted">two pairs</span> of prescribed basepoints lying on two distinct fibers of the natural projection <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\colon{\bf F}_{g_{v}}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\colon{\bf F}_{g_{v}}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. (We need two pairs of points to glue this family with the rest of the admissible cover as dictated by the altered dual graph above.)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">The resulting test family <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> provides the relation we seek because it has negative intersection with <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> and with two other higher boundary divisors, each having smaller excess. (<math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> also interacts with enumeratively relevant divisors.)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">If the divisor <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is ramified, we consider two cases. First, suppose there is a vertex <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, such that locally around <math id="S2.SS14.SSS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> the dual graph has the form:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

