<tbody id="S4.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{{\mathsf{X}}}\cdot p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖷</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{{\mathsf{X}}}\cdot p</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">By intersecting with <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{X}}=a\lambda-b\delta-{{\mathsf{Y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖷</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝖸</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{X}}=a\lambda-b\delta-{{\mathsf{Y}}}</annotation></semantics></math> we deduce <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta_{0},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta_{0},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">The analysis for <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> odd is completely analogous. We simply need to show that <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta_{1},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta_{1},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> has an elliptic curve as the right hand component. Again, we just use a partial pencil family on on the surface <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We leave the details to the reader.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">4.1.3 <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-vertex divisors II.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If we consider modified versions of the partial pencil <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> in the previous section, we obtain slightly different numbers. Suppose we impose a subscheme of type <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{2p_{1},p_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{2p_{1},p_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math> in a ruling line <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\subset{\bf F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>𝐅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\subset{\bf F}</annotation></semantics></math> to be in the base locus of <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\subset|{\mathcal{O}}_{{\bf F}}(C)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>𝐅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}_{t}\subset|{\mathcal{O}}_{{\bf F}}(C)|</annotation></semantics></math> as in section <a href="#S2.SS12.SSS5" title="2.12.5 Variation on the basic construction I. ‣ 2.12 Constructions of partial pencils. ‣ 2 Compactifications. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.12.5</span></a>. Then we will have two special fibers: the split fiber, corresponding to interaction with a divisor <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{{\rm split}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>split</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{{\rm split}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the reduced ramification fiber corresponding to intersection with a divisor <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{{\rm ram}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ram</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{{\rm ram}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote the resulting partial pencil by <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to distinguish it from the pencil <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> from proposition <a href="#S4.Thmthm1" title="Proposition 4.1. ‣ 4.1.1 
            
              2
            
          -vertex divisors I. ‣ 4.1 Degree three analysis. ‣ 4 The slope problem. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, and let <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> denote the boundary divisor which contains <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We have:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.6</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The partial pencil <math id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> has the following intersection numbers:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda\cdot p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda\cdot p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g_{R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta\cdot p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta\cdot p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=7g_{R}+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=7g_{R}+4</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\cdot p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\cdot p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{{\rm split}}\cdot p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>split</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{{\rm split}}\cdot p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{{\rm ram}}\cdot p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ram</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{{\rm ram}}\cdot p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathsf{X}}\cdot p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖷</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathsf{X}}\cdot p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The only number needing explanation is <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\cdot p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\cdot p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. We must subtract <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7g_{R}+6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7g_{R}+6</annotation></semantics></math> because there are now two gluing sections in the partial pencil, each with self intersection <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">4.1.4 Inequalities II.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.SS1.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> be a simply ramified <math id="S4.SS1.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-vertex divisor with dual graph <math id="S4.SS1.SSS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.Ex21.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="29.86" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-15.051833686284938px" version="1.1" viewBox="22.55 15.05 124.11 29.86" width="124.11"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 22.554884515099626 29.857672974663156) translate(0,3.46) translate(22.56,0)"><g transform="translate(-3.46,0) translate(0,-3.07)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.44em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.15)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex21.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\bullet}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\bullet}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(-22.56,0) translate(0,7.87) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.95em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.56" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="13.19"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex21.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\scriptstyle v_{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">v</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\scriptstyle v_{L}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(-22.49,0) translate(0,-7.87) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.14)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.94em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.05" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="13.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="l