<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Clearly, there are two types of <math id="S4.SS1.SSS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-vertex divisors: either <math id="S4.SS1.SSS7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is ramified, or not. We will only consider the analysis for the unramified case - the reader will by now be able to make the necessary minor adjustments for the ramified case.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We vary the genus <math id="S4.SS1.SSS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> hyperelliptic curve associated to node <math id="S4.SS1.SSS7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> in a <math id="S4.SS1.SSS7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> pencil on <math id="S4.SS1.SSS7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}_{g_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}_{g_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> with two specified points <math id="S4.SS1.SSS7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},p_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},p_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> on a ruling line <math id="S4.SS1.SSS7.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> lying in the base locus. The resulting partial pencil, <math id="S4.SS1.SSS7.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, will intersect a new boundary divisor <math id="S4.SS1.SSS7.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{{\rm split}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>split</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{{\rm split}}</annotation></semantics></math> which has dual graph <math id="S4.SS1.SSS7.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{\Delta_{{\rm split}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>split</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{\Delta_{{\rm split}}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
