<p id="S4.SS1.SSS8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">As usual in such symmetric settings, we assume <math id="S4.SS1.SSS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{R}\leq g_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{R}\leq g_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. Again, vary <math id="S4.SS1.SSS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> in a partial pencil of hyperelliptic curves. We obtain a family of admissible covers <math id="S4.SS1.SSS8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> which intersects one other higher boundary divisor <math id="S4.SS1.SSS8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{{\rm split}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>split</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{{\rm split}}</annotation></semantics></math> whose dual graph is <math id="S4.SS1.SSS8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{\Delta_{{\rm split}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>split</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{\Delta_{{\rm split}}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
