<p id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Assume that <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{L}\geq g_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{L}\geq g_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By imposing <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> distinct points <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{1},p_{2},p_{3},p_{4}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{1},p_{2},p_{3},p_{4}\}</annotation></semantics></math> in a fiber <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\subset{\bf F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>𝐅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\subset{\bf F}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then attaching a constant left side cover <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{L}{\colon}C_{L}\longrightarrow P_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{L}{\colon}C_{L}\longrightarrow P_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, we construct a partial pencil <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> lying entirely inside a boundary divisor <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The split fiber <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{{\rm split}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>split</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{{\rm split}}</annotation></semantics></math> has dual graph <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{\Delta_{{\rm split}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>split</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{\Delta_{{\rm split}}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
