<tbody id="S4.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\cdot p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\cdot p</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{{\rm split}}\cdot p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>split</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{{\rm split}}\cdot p</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex57.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathsf{X}}\cdot p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖷</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathsf{X}}\cdot p</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex58.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">This follows easily from the calculations in <a href="#S3.Thmthm18" title="Proposition 3.18. ‣ 3.11.3 ‣ 3.11 Constructing families of tetragonal curves. ‣ 3 One parameter families and . ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.18</span></a>. The last inequality follows from the fact that such partial pencils <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> pass through the general point of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm23" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm23.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.23</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm23.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm23.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm23.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the setting of the previous proposition, we have the following inequality:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta,{\mathsf{Y}})\geq c(\Delta_{{\rm split}},{{\mathsf{Y}}})+b(v+6g_{R}+2)-a(g_{R})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>split</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta,{\mathsf{Y}})\geq c(\Delta_{{\rm split}},{{\mathsf{Y}}})+b(v+6g_{R}+2)-a(g_{R}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We intersect <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS3.SSS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{X}}=a\lambda-b\delta-{\mathsf{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖷</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝖸</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{X}}=a\lambda-b\delta-{\mathsf{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">4.3.2 A hitch in the induction.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{a}{b}=\frac{13g+15}{2g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{a}{b}=\frac{13g+15}{2g}</annotation></semantics></math>. Unfortunately, we may not run the induction procedure directly from <a href="#S4.Thmthm23" title="Lemma 4.23. ‣ 4.3.1 Unramified, 
            
              2
            
          -vertex 
            
              Δ
            
          . ‣ 4.3 Degree four analysis. ‣ 4 The slope problem. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.23</span></a> as we did in the degree three analysis: the quantity</p>
<table id="S4.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(v+6g_{R}+2)-a(g_{R})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(v+6g_{R}+2)-a(g_{R})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is not positive for all <math id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> in the assumed range <math id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{R}\leq(g-3)/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{R}\leq(g-3)/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Luckily, the fraction of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>’s making this quantity negative is quite small, so we can use <a href="#S4.Thmthm23" title="Lemma 4.23. ‣ 4.3.1 Unramified, 
            
              2
            
          -vertex 
            
              Δ
            
          . ‣ 4.3 Degree four analysis. ‣ 4 The slope problem. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.23</span></a> multiple times, reducing genera of the vertex <math id="S4.SS3.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> by three each time, and add all the resulting inequalities. This strategy ends up working, as we explain next.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">4.3.3 </h4>

<div id="S4.Thmthm24" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.24</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm24.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm24.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm24.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the setting above, we have:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta,{\mathsf{Y}})\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta,{\mathsf{Y}})\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{R}=3i+k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{R}=3i+k</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0,1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0,1,2</annotation></semantics></math> depending on <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{R}\mod 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{R}\mod 3</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the unramified, <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-vertex boundary divisor having dual graph <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{\Delta_{l}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{\Delta_{l}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.Ex62.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="34.01" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-19.901941240584353px" version="1.1" viewBox="18.90 19.90 125.45 34.01" width="125.45"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 18.903416387764633 34.01208784927615) translate(0,3.46) translate(18.9,0)"><g transform="translate(-3.46,0) translate(0,-3.07)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.44em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.15)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex62.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\bullet}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\bullet}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(-18.9,0) translate(0,7.87) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-2.09)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.43em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="4.17" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="5.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex62.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\scriptstyle v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\scriptstyle v}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(75.28,0) translate(0,-3.07)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.44em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.15)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex62.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\bull