<p id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">(So our original boundary divisor <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.) <a href="#S4.Thmthm23" title="Lemma 4.23. ‣ 4.3.1 Unramified, 
            
              2
            
          -vertex 
            
              Δ
            
          . ‣ 4.3 Degree four analysis. ‣ 4 The slope problem. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.23</span></a> gives:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta_{l},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq c(\Delta_{l-1},{{\mathsf{Y}}})+b(v_{l}+6(3l+k)+2)-a(3l+k)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta_{l},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq c(\Delta_{l-1},{{\mathsf{Y}}})+b(v_{l}+6(3l+k)+2)-a(3l+k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>. We may add these relations together for <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq l\leq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq l\leq i</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain the following expression</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta_{i},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq c(\Delta_{0},{{\mathsf{Y}}})+\displaystyle{\sum_{l=1}^{i}(18b-3a)l}+bv_{l}+(6bk+2b-ka)i" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta_{i},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq c(\Delta_{0},{{\mathsf{Y}}})+\displaystyle{\sum_{l=1}^{i}(18b-3a)l}+bv_{l}+(6bk+2b-ka)i</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">In the above expression, <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{l}:=\lceil{\frac{3l+k+3}{2}\rceil}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{l}:=\lceil{\frac{3l+k+3}{2}\rceil}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, if we replace <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{3l+k+3}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{3l+k+3}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and if the sum in the right hand side of (<a href="#S4.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.3.3 ‣ 4.3 Degree four analysis. ‣ 4 The slope problem. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.6</span></a>) remains positive, we will be able to deduce the inequality <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta,{\mathsf{Y}})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta,{\mathsf{Y}})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> from the inequality <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta_{0},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta_{0},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, substituting <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{3l+k+3}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{3l+k+3}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta_{i},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq c(\Delta_{0},{{\mathsf{Y}}})+3\left(\frac{13}{2}b-a\right)\cdot{i+1\choose 2}+\left(\left(\frac{13}{2}k+\frac{7}{2}\right)b-ka\right)\cdot i" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta_{i},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq c(\Delta_{0},{{\mathsf{Y}}})+3\left(\frac{13}{2}b-a\right)\cdot{i+1\choose 2}+\left(\left(\frac{13}{2}k+\frac{7}{2}\right)b-ka\right)\cdot i</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">From here, it is straightforward to check that</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\left(\frac{13}{2}b-a\right){i+1\choose 2}+\left(\left(\frac{13}{2}k+\frac{7}{2}\right)b-ka\right)i\geq 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\left(\frac{13}{2}b-a\right){i+1\choose 2}+\left(\left(\frac{13}{2}k+\frac{7}{2}\right)b-ka\right)i\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">for <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> in the required range, i.e. <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3i+k\leq\frac{g-3}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3i+k\leq\frac{g-3}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we must only show that <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta_{0},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta_{0},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. These remaining cases are easily dealt with if we simply interpret the divisor <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> as having more than <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> vertices.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">In other words, the split fibers appearing in the partial pencils in the analysis of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta_{0},{\mathsf{Y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta_{0},{\mathsf{Y}})</annotation></semantics></math> have disconnected residual curves. However, as we explained earlier, we know <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta_{-1},0)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta_{-1},0)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. The relation</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta_{0},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq c(\Delta_{-1},{{\mathsf{Y}}})+b(v_{0}+6k+2)-ak" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta_{0},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq c(\Delta_{-1},{{\mathsf{Y}}})+b(v_{0}+6k+2)-ak</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">then allows us to conclude <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta_{0},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta_{0},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, since the quantity <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(v_{0}+6k+2)-ak" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(v_{0}+6k+2)-ak</annotation></semantics></math> is positive for these small values for <math id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, as the reader can check.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">4.3.4 Ramified, <math id="S4.SS3.SSS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-vertex divisors.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The rest of the degree four analysis goes through without any hitches.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We modify the basic pencil <math id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> above by imposing nonreduced base points as we did in the degree three case. We will demonstrate the analysis in one case, and leave the remaining cases to the reader.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be the partial pencil obtained by imposing a <math id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>-tuple of basepoints of the form <math id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{2p_{1},p_{2},p_{3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{2p_{1},p_{2},p_{3}\}</annotation></semantics></math> in a general conic fiber of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\colon{\bf F}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\colon{\bf F}\longrightarrow{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

