<p id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S4.Thmthm24" title="Proposition 4.24. ‣ 4.3.3 ‣ 4.3 Degree four analysis. ‣ 4 The slope problem. ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.24</span></a><span id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">says <math id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta_{{\rm split}},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>split</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta_{{\rm split}},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta_{{\rm ram}},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ram</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta_{{\rm ram}},{{\mathsf{Y}}})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By intersecting <math id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{X}}=a\lambda-b\delta-{\mathsf{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖷</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝖸</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{X}}=a\lambda-b\delta-{\mathsf{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta,{\mathsf{Y}})\geq c(\Delta_{{\rm split}},{{\mathsf{Y}}})+c(\Delta_{{\rm ram}},{{\mathsf{Y}}})+9g-15g_{R}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>split</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ram</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta,{\mathsf{Y}})\geq c(\Delta_{{\rm split}},{{\mathsf{Y}}})+c(\Delta_{{\rm ram}},{{\mathsf{Y}}})+9g-15g_{R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since we assume <math id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{R}\leq\frac{g-3}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{R}\leq\frac{g-3}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we easily conclude that <math id="S4.SS3.SSS4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\Delta,{\mathsf{Y}})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\Delta,{\mathsf{Y}})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">4.3.5 Higher ramification.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For higher ramification, we simply impose more nonreduced points in the base loci of our partial pencils. The resulting partial pencil family will relate the current ramified divisor <math id="S4.SS3.SSS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> with a divisor <math id="S4.SS3.SSS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{{\rm ram}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ram</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{{\rm ram}}</annotation></semantics></math> having less ramification. We omit the details to avoid repetitiveness.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">4.4 Degree five analysis.</h3>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our approach to the degree five case of <a href="#S3.Thmthm7" title="Theorem 3.7 (Key result for ). ‣ 3.7 The key result. ‣ 3 One parameter families and . ‣ Special Codimension One Loci in Hurwitz Spaces" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>, although similar in essence to the previous two, has one added complication. So far, we have never had to compute the exact intersection number of a partial pencil with the divisors <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{CE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖢𝖤</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{CE}}</annotation></semantics></math> – it was always sufficient only to know that these intersections were nonnegative.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the degree five case, we will have to understand intersections of partial pencils with the Maroni divisor <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>. (Our choice of partial pencil will conveniently circumvent any need to consider <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{CE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖢𝖤</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{CE}}</annotation></semantics></math>.)</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=5</annotation></semantics></math>, the reader can check that the coefficients <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> occurring in the divisor class expression for <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathsf{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖷</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathsf{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> are:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex76.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(31g+44)/10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>31</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>44</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(31g+44)/10</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex77.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g/2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g/2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">4.4.1 Unramified, <math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-vertex divisors.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by considering a boundary divisor <math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> whose dual graph <math id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S4.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.Ex78.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="29.86" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-15.051833686284938px" version="1.1" viewBox="22.55 15.05 124.11 29.86" width="124.11"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 22.554884515099626 29.857672974663156) translate(0,3.46) translate(22.56,0)"><g transform="translate(-3.46,0) translate(0,-3.07)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.44em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.15)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex78.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\bullet}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\bullet}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(-22.56,0) translate(0,7.87) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.95em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.56" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="13.19"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex78.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\scriptstyle v_{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">v</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\scriptstyle v_{L}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(-22.49,0) translate(0,-7.87) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.14)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.94em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.05" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="13.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="l